	You're right.  You were wrong.  ;-)

	S'pose you find a WOW with three charges.  Okay, you blow one wishing
	for a BSOC.  You have two wishes left.

	After those two are gone, you charge the WOW with the BSOC.  You now
	have three more wishes.

	Once these are gone, you can, with effort, wrest a final wish from the
	wand, and then it crumbles.  So, if you start off _without_ a blessed
	scroll of charging, you effectively have six wishes from a WOW.  If
	you have the BSOC, you got seven, total.  If you start off with a
	USOC, you get a max of 5.



